 <name>perfidious</name>
 <channel>pecl.php.net</channel>
 <summary>Access Linux and Windows performance counters</summary>
 <description>This extension provides access to Linux perf_events and low-level Windows performance monitoring counters.</description>
 <lead>
  <name>John Boehr</name>
  <user>jbboehr</user>
  <email>jbboehr@gmail.com</email>
  <active>yes</active>
 </lead>
 <date>2026-08-01</date>
 <version>
  <release>0.2.0</release>
  <api>0.2.0</api>
 </version>
 <stability>
  <release>beta</release>
  <api>beta</api>
 </stability>
 <license uri="https://spdx.org/licenses/romic-exception.html">AGPL-3.0-only WITH romic-exception</license>
 <notes>
  - Added: support for PHP 8.5.
  - Added: a static-linked ASan/UBSan build for sanitizer testing.
  - Added: a NixOS VM test covering perfidious.global.enable / perfidious.request.enable
    persistence under php-fpm.
  - Changed: relicensed from AGPL-3.0-or-later to AGPL-3.0-only WITH romic-exception, a linking
    exception permitting this extension to be linked into other code without that code becoming
    subject to the AGPL. See docs/LICENSE_EXCEPTION.md and CONTRIBUTING.md.
  - Changed: Perfidious\open() now rejects more than 1000 event names with
    Perfidious\OverflowException, instead of accepting an unbounded array.
  - Fixed: a memory leak where the handle's underlying native struct was never freed when a
    Handle was closed or garbage collected.
  - Fixed: Handle::rawStream() closing the returned stream no longer closes the handle's own
    file descriptor out from under it.
  - Fixed: -Werror no longer defaults on for a plain git-checkout build, only inside the
    project's own nix devShell.
  - Security: fixed stack buffer over-reads that could leak adjacent stack memory into a
    PmuEventInfo object's $name property, or into exception/warning messages, for
    PMU/event name combinations long enough to overflow an internal formatting buffer.
 </notes>
